std::string s("ab") -- construction from a string literal.

FRONT-END CONFORMANCE established: with the member-typedef conformance fix
([temp.inst]/1-2, [dcl.typedef], [class.prop]), basic_string<char> is no longer
truncated at its const_reverse_iterator member typedef, so it keeps its
constructors, is not misclassified as a POD, and the (const char*) constructor
is selected.  This reaches Bounded Model Checking with NO CONVERSION ERROR (the
forbidden patterns above guard that conformance).

Remains KNOWNBUG only because BMC of the fully-elaborated libstdc++ basic_string
exhausts resources before VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL -- a second-tier
verification-PERFORMANCE item (symex on real libstdc++ containers), not a
conformance gap.  Reclassify to CORE once std::string construction is
BMC-tractable.
